# Electroduplicate's flashback {2}{R}{R} (CR 702.34a, 707.9a): after the spell from hand, Bot1 flashes it back targeting the token
# it made. The new token copies the first token, so it has the same haste and sacrifice ability as copiable values (not only an
# effect's haste): both tokens attack and are sacrificed at the end step. Electroduplicate is exiled, not put back in the graveyard.
[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus x3
Mons's Goblin Raiders
Electroduplicate
Mountain x2
Mountain x10
[Bot2 Deck]
Plains x20
[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus#1.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus#1.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus#1.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Mons's Goblin Raiders.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Electroduplicate.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Mons's Goblin Raiders)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Graveyard.Electroduplicate.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Mons's Goblin Raiders#2; Ability: Flashback)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Exile.Count = 1
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mons's Goblin Raiders#3.Token = true
? Bot1.Battlefield.Mons's Goblin Raiders#3.Keywords = Haste
Bot1.Attack(Mons's Goblin Raiders#2; Mons's Goblin Raiders#3 > Bot2)
[T1 Bot1.Main2]
? Bot2.Life = 18
[T2 Bot2.Main1]

[Expect]
Bot2.Life = 18
Exile.Count = 1
Bot1.Battlefield = Mons's Goblin Raiders
